# Throwaway Compose project rs27-mini (mini/compose.yaml): Rakazo v0.4.0 supervisor (ghcr.io/elie222/rakazo/app:v0.4.0,
# computer image ghcr.io/elie222/rakazo/computer:v0.4.0), the egress sidecar from Rakazo's docs ("Docker in a Linux VM")
# running the unmodified v0.4.0 restrict-computer-egress.sh (sha256 c2802eef…c3), an alpine "relay-standin" and an alpine
# "web" stand-in, both on an ordinary Compose network. SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted throughout.
# Windows 11 (build 26300), Docker Desktop 4.97.0 (244584), Engine 29.9.2, WSL 2 backend, WSL networking mode nat.
# Listener: Windows' python.exe http.server bound to Windows' 127.0.0.1:18927 (win-listener.sh). The live Instance's
# web/api are published on Windows' 127.0.0.1:5173/3100. Supervisor token generated per run, not shown.
# Computers created and probed with compose-boot's computer-probe.sh (TCP connect, 3 s timeout, via the supervisor's
# exec API) and probe-all targets; machine-specific addresses replaced with <placeholders>.

## 1. Boot with SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted
