SSH banner (SSH-2.0) reads, 8 s timeout:
  WSL distro github.com:22 10/10; WSL distro ssh.github.com:443 10/10; computer ssh.github.com:443 10/10
  then, same method run at the same time: WSL distro 0/20, restricted computer 0/20, unrestricted computer image on default bridge 0/20
=> port-22 failures hit the unrestricted container and the WSL distro as well (GitHub throttling this public IP after the
   repeated probes); the rules do not block SSH. SSH banners from the restricted computer did succeed on :22 and :443.

## 2. Relay path (relay-standin, ordinary Compose network, br-*)
http://host.docker.internal:18927/       ok      (Windows 127.0.0.1 listener)
http://supervisor:7091/health            ok
supervisor:7091                          open
1.1.1.1:443                              open

rules in Docker Desktop's engine namespace (vm-rules.sh list):
-A DOCKER-USER -i rakazo-c+ -o rakazo-c+ -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -d 0.0.0.0/8 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 10.0.0.0/8 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 100.64.0.0/10 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 127.0.0.0/8 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 169.254.0.0/16 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 172.16.0.0/12 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 192.0.0.0/24 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 192.168.0.0/16 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 198.18.0.0/15 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 224.0.0.0/4 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -d 240.0.0.0/4 -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i eth0 -j ACCEPT                                         (Docker Desktop's own rules from here down)
-A DOCKER-USER -i eth1 -j ACCEPT
-A DOCKER-USER ! -i eth0 -o services1 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 3128 -j ACCEPT
-A DOCKER-USER ! -i eth0 -o services1 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 5555 -j ACCEPT
-A DOCKER-USER ! -i eth0 -o services1 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT
-A DOCKER-USER ! -i eth0 -o services1 -p tcp -j REJECT --reject-with icmp-port-unreachable
-A INPUT -i rakazo-c+ -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP
ip6tables DOCKER-USER: the same RETURN plus drops for ::1/128 fc00::/7 fe80::/10 ff00::/8

