## 4. Rules removed while the supervisor keeps running (restricted verdict already cached)
compose stop computer-egress; vm-rules.sh remove -> rakazo-c+ rules: v4 0 (INPUT 0), v6 0
computer-probe.sh create rs27bot2 -> 200 {"id":"2ea57c78…","resumed":false}   bridge name rakazo-cc9a4142
host.docker.internal:18927         open       <- computer reaches Windows 127.0.0.1
host.docker.internal:5173          open       <- and the published web port
169.254.169.254:80                 refused/unresolved
1.1.1.1:443                        open
=> restricted checks once per supervisor lifetime (restrictedEgressVerified, index.ts L1224-L1253); it does not
   re-check later provisions, so it fails closed only until the first pass.

## 5. Supervisor restarted with the rules missing (fail closed)
compose restart supervisor
supervisor log 08:21:04 {"level":"error","message":"restricted computer egress unavailable","error":{"message":"SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted is not enforced on this Docker host: …"}}
computer-probe.sh create rs27bot3 ->
500 {"error":"SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted is not enforced on this Docker host: run infra/compose/restrict-computer-egress.sh on the host, or set SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=open (see docs/self-host-docker-computers.md) (a computer bridge reached the host)"}

## 6. Sidecar started again, supervisor NOT restarted
08:21:28 compose start computer-egress; 08:21:29 rakazo-c+ rules: v4 14 (INPUT 2), v6 7
computer-probe.sh create rs27bot3 -> 200 {"id":"59ee059f…","resumed":false}
host.docker.internal:18927 timeout, host.docker.internal:5173 timeout, 1.1.1.1:443 open, example.com:443 open
rs27bot2 (created in step 4 while the rules were missing; still running on its rakazo-c bridge):
host.docker.internal:18927 timeout, host.docker.internal:5173 timeout, 1.1.1.1:443 open
=> the rules key on the bridge name, so they cover computers created while they were missing as soon as they return.
